Selected T8010 SmartIO, DMA, SPI and touchscreen support in the J71b kernel
patches and modules incorporates or adapts work by Paul Praschl (Pauli1Go):
https://github.com/Pauli1Go/HoolockLinux
Reference revision: d49ac41cb898881457a97bb3cd44b7d92ff50a8c.
The J71b firmware startup sequence was adapted from the J172 implementation;
firmware packet validation also follows Pauli1Go's makez2fw format:
https://github.com/Pauli1Go/HoolockLinux-linux-firmware
Reference revision: 944541e67b4c603df328c77d30093551de802c17.
Original copyright notices and per-file licenses remain applicable. This is
selective reuse and adaptation, not a replacement of the pinned base kernel.

The opt-in J71b source-aware charging policy adapts Berkay Kösebay's linux-a9
charge7 (kernel a8aa6fea363394f3d21f2eef7525998884b4cf3f), reconstructed from
Apple's iOS D2365/CBTL1610 charging paths. It retains OrchardLinux's J71b lease
ownership, battery guards, runtime and PM-safe handoff, on the HoolockLinux /
Pauli1Go platform groundwork credited above. No Apple firmware, decompilation
or per-unit calibration is distributed with this policy.

